在各大播客平台关注并收听由梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的“我们毫不在乎俱乐部”播客。

294
00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:37.610
Well, we are back, and today's episode was inspired by Emily L.
好了，我们回来了，今天的节目灵感来自圣迭戈的埃米莉·L.

295
00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.630
from San Diego, who wrote
她写信提出了以下问题。

296
00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.010
in with the following question.
她写信提出了以下问题。

297
00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:42.390
Hi, office ladies.
嗨，办公室女士们。

298
00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:46.570
I'd love to learn more about your office trailers over the years as it's a behind-the-scenes
我很想多了解一下你们这些年来在《办公室》剧组的休息车，因为这是我们知之甚少的幕后拍摄地点。

299
00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.170
location we know little about.
因为这是我们知之甚少的幕后拍摄地点。

300
00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.370
Did you have to pack up your trailer at the end of the season?
你们在每一季结束时都必须把休息车里的东西打包带走吗？

301
00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.430
Were you able to pick your neighbors?
你能选你的邻居吗？

302
00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:57.430
And were there any particularly special personal items you kept in yours over the years?
这些年来，你有没有在自己的房间里保存过什么特别的私人物品？

303
00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:00.790
Here's hoping you hitch this question to a future episode.
希望你们能在以后的单集里聊聊这个问题。

304
00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:02.510
All the best, Emily.
祝好，艾米。

305
00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:08.530
Well, Emily, not only did we hitch this question to a future episode, we made a whole episode
嗯，艾米，我们不仅在以后的节目里聊了这个，我们还专门做了一整集

306
00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:09.110
out of it.
来讨论它。

307
00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.950
So here we go.
所以我们开始吧。

308
00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.170
Emily, this really got us excited.
艾米，这真的让我们很兴奋。

309
00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.570
We were deep-diving old photos.
我们深入翻看了旧照片。

310
00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.910
Angela, you found some videos that you took in our trailers.
安吉拉，你还找到了你在我们化妆车里拍的一些视频。

311
00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:24.110
I thought we should kick things off by describing the different kinds of trailers.
我觉得我们应该先介绍一下不同种类的化妆车。

312
00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:25.770
Oh, that's so smart.
哦，这太聪明了。

313
00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.710
Yes, there are categories of trailers.
是的，化妆车也是分种类的。

314
00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:31.890
So the first category of trailer is called a honey wagon.
所以第一种化妆车叫做“蜜月车”（多功能拖车）。

315
00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:37.530
And this is like a large trailer that is divided into tiny dressing rooMs.
这就像是一个分隔成许多小化妆间的大型拖车。

316
00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:40.250
Not much bigger than what you might find at the mall.
比你在商场试衣间里看到的也大不了多少。

317
00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:45.850
If you're lucky, there's a tiny bench that you can sit on.
如果运气好的话，里面会有一个可以坐的小长凳。

318
00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:46.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

319
00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:54.230
Then there's like a little teeny rack to hang clothes and maybe a sink and maybe a toilet.
然后有一个像微型衣架一样的东西用来挂衣服，可能还有一个洗手池和一个马桶。

320
00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:55.150
Maybe, yeah.
也许有，对。

321
00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:55.710
Maybe.
也许吧。

322
00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:56.650
But sometimes not.
但有时也没有。

323
00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.210
Sometimes it's just the bench and a little clothing rack.
有时就只有长凳和一个小衣架。

324
00:15:59.430 --> 00:15:59.850
Yes.
是的。

325
00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:05.110
And this is what you are likely going to be put in for your first acting role.
而这很可能是你接演第一个演艺角色时会被安排到的地方。

326
00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:10.550
If you've got a couple of lines, if you're there for one day, you get the honey wagon.
如果你只有几句台词，只拍一天，你就会被安排在蜜月车里。

327
00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.090
Or if you're doing like a very low-budget project.
或者如果你是在拍那种非常低成本的项目。

328
00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:14.650
Exactly.
没错。

329
00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:23.810
When we did Lee's movie, that was, you know, an indie film, we were in a honey wagon to change clothes.
当我们拍李的电影时，你知道，那是一部独立电影，我们就是在一个蜜月车里换衣服。

330
00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:24.210
Everybody.
每个人都是。

331
00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:25.790
We all had a honey wagon.
我们全都在蜜月车里。

332
00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:28.370
There was no like, oh, so-and-so has a bigger space.
没有什么“哦，某某的空间比较大”这种说法。

333
00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:30.050
No, we were all in a honey wagon.
没有，我们全都在蜜月车里。

334
00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.250
Everybody got honey wagons.
每个人都有蜜月车。

335
00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:35.990
And you know, Kate Flannery and I were in a honey wagon season one of The Office.
你知道的，《办公室》第一季时，我和凯特·弗兰内里就在一个蜜月车里。

336
00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:37.990
But you guys had toilets.
但你们有马桶。

337
00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.210
Okay, here is the weirdest thing.
好吧，最诡异的事来了。

338
00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:45.490
We were in a honey wagon, and I think I've talked about this before, but the only thing
我们在一个蜜月车里，我想我以前说过这个，但唯一隔开

339
00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:50.350
that separated her bench and her toilet from my bench and my toilet was an accordion door.
她的长凳和马桶与我的长凳和马桶的，是一个折叠门。

340
00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:52.870
Which is so wild to me.
这让我觉得太离谱了。

341
00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:58.210
And the accordion door was made out of like flimsy plastic, and it had a magnet that never
而且这个折叠门是用那种劣质塑料做的，上面还有一个从来

342
00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:58.910
attached.
吸不上的磁铁。

343
00:16:59.290 --> 00:16:59.590
Yes.
对。

344
00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:03.490
So we just decided on day one, okay, here are the rules.
所以我们从第一天就决定，好吧，规矩是这样的。

345
00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:07.230
We are going to keep the accordion door open because what's the point?
我们要一直把折叠门开着，因为开着有什么意义呢？

346
00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:09.370
Like, I can hear everything you're doing.
总之，你干的每件事我都听得见。

347
00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:13.330
And we made a vow to never use either toilet.
而且我们发誓绝对不用里面任何一个马桶。

348
00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:19.850
I mean, these are important foundries that I think you set that were very smart.
我的意思是，我觉得你们当时立下的这些界限非常明智。

349
00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:24.150
So we just kept the lids closed, and I like put like a plant on mine.
所以我们只是把马桶盖盖上，我还喜欢在上面放一盆植物。

350
00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:24.910
Yeah.
对。

351
00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:27.330
I have a picture that, you know, I cherish.
我有一张照片，你知道的，我非常珍视。

352
00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:28.290
It's in our book.
它就在我们的书里。

353
00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:33.350
And we have a lot of fun pictures in our book from this time on set and the behind the scenes.
我们的书里有很多那个时期片场和幕后的有趣照片。

354
00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.910
So, you know, little shout out for The Office BFFs.
所以，你知道的，给《办公室好闺蜜》做个小小的宣传。

355
00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:39.670
But I do have that picture of me and Kate in our honey wagon.
但我确实有那张我和凯特在化妆车里的照片。

356
00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:46.810
Well, after you graduate from the honey wagon, then you get into what is called either a triple
嗯，从化妆车毕业后，你就会住进所谓的

357
00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.050
banger, a double banger, or a single.
三人间、双人间或单人间。

358
00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:50.710
I don't know why that's what they're called.
我不知道为什么它们叫这个名字。

359
00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:56.830
But they are what they sound like, which is that you can have a trailer and it's divided into three
但它们就像听起来的那样，你可以拥有一个拖车，里面分成三个

360
00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:01.770
different dressing rooms, or a double banger is divided into two different dressing rooMs.
不同的化妆间，或者双人间分成两个不同的化妆间。

361
00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:04.370
And then a single is just like, you get the whole thing.
然后单人间就像是，你一个人用整间。

362
00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:05.350
Yeah.
是的。

363
00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:08.850
Now, I will say, even with a triple banger, it's a huge upgrade.
现在我要说，即使是三人间，也是一个巨大的升级。

364
00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:12.370
Because that's what Kate and I and everyone else in the supporting cast got season two.
因为那是第二季我和凯特以及其他配角得到的待遇。

365
00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:14.730
And I mean, it was like Shangri-La.
我的意思是，那简直就像香格里拉。

366
00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:15.870
We had a bench.
我们有一个长凳。

367
00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.570
We had a little mini fridge.
我们有一个小迷你冰箱。

368
00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:23.030
We had a little vanity and a bathroom and a tiny TV that never worked.
我们有一个小梳妆台、一个卫生间和一个从来没管用过的小电视。

369
00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:27.070
And the microwave, one time I used it and I thought I was going to burn everything because
至于微波炉，我有一次用它，以为要把一切都烧了

370
00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:27.890
it started smoking.
因为它开始冒烟了。

371
00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:32.250
So, I didn't use my appliances, but it was a lot more space.
所以，我没有用我的电器，但空间大多了。

372
00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:32.670
Yeah.
是的。

373
00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:39.370
Well, from the time I started on The Office until almost the end, I was in a double banger.
嗯，从我开始拍《办公室》到快结束时，我都住在双人间里。

374
00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:44.350
So, I was in a trailer divided into two different big dressing rooMs.
所以我住在一个分成两个不同大化妆间的拖车里。

375
00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.530
And I had a lot of space.
我有很多空间。

376
00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:49.890
I had a really nice, like, sort of a couch, right?
我有一个非常好的，怎么说呢，类似沙发的家具，对吧？

377
00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:52.950
That's why we would eat lunch in your trailer because you had a table.
这就是为什么我们总是在你的化妆车里吃午饭，因为你有一张桌子。

378
00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.010
I had a table.
我有一张桌子。

379
00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.050
I also had a TV that did not work.
我还有一个同样不好使的电视。

380
00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:58.990
And wait, you know what, lady?
等等，你知道吗，女士？

381
00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.710
Before your table, we had TV trays.
在你有桌子之前，我们用的是电视托盘桌。

382
00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:02.690
And then I remember we came back one season.
然后我记得有一次我们过完季回来。

383
00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:05.630
It was like after the holidays and all of a sudden they'd put a table.
就像是假期过后，突然之间他们放了一张桌子。

384
00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:06.910
And we were so excited.
我们当时可太兴奋了。

385
00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:07.990
I remember that.
我记得那个。

386
00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:13.490
And then you had like a bathroom that had a shower and it had a toilet.
然后你有一个带淋浴和马桶的浴室。

387
00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.070
Did you ever use the shower?
你用过那个淋浴间吗？

388
00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:19.570
I had to use it once.
我不得不用过一次。

389
00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:24.570
And I can't remember what the episode was, but I was messy.
我不记得是哪一集了，但我当时弄得很脏。

390
00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.530
I don't know why I needed to use it, but I did.
我不知道为什么我得用它，但我确实用了。

391
00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:32.050
But the thing is that it's like, you know, it's not warm.
但问题是，你知道的，它一点也不暖和。

392
00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:33.170
Yeah.
是的。

393
00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.370
It's like a campsite shower.
就像露营地的淋浴间。

394
00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.810
Like in an RV park kind of shower.
就像房车营地那种淋浴间。

395
00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:38.490
Exactly.
完全正确。

396
00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.650
If you've ever seen an RV bathroom, they were very similar.
如果你见过房车浴室，它们非常相似。

397
00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.230
And like you have to flush the toilet.
而且你得冲马桶。

398
00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.230
You have to push a pedal, you know, on the ground.
你得踩地上的一个踏板，你知道的。

399
00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:45.770
Yes.
是的。

400
00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:53.790
And the first time I finally had a trailer that I could go to the bathroom in, I could not
而且当我有生以来第一次拥有一个可以在里面上厕所的拖车时，我简直无法

401
00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.570
find how to flush it, lady.
去找找怎么冲水，莱迪。

402
00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:57.710
I looked everywhere for a handle.
我到处找冲水把手。

403
00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:00.330
No one told me to look on the floor.
没人告诉我把手在地上。

404
00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:05.210
And I remember I had to go ask someone, I had to be like, hey, you have a toilet?
我还记得我不得不去问别人，我就像，嘿，你们有厕所吗？

405
00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:05.970
How do you flush?
怎么冲水？

406
00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:07.090
Yes.
对。

407
00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:11.510
Well, something people should know is that your trailer is part of your contract.
好吧，人们应该知道的一点是，你的化妆车是合同的一部分。

408
00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:17.690
So like when your agent calls you and says you got the job, they'll say like, here's your
所以，当你的经纪人打电话告诉你得到这份工作时，他们会说，这是你的

409
00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:18.190
salary.
薪水。

410
00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:20.270
Here's the number of days you'll be working.
这是你的工作天数。

411
00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:21.830
Here are the dates.
这是日期。

412
00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:24.290
And you're going to be in a triple banger.
然后你会住进一间三人间化妆车。

413
00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:26.250
I never knew that.
我以前不知道这个。

414
00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:33.390
So basically, like, f*** my agent for putting me in a money wagon in season one of The Office.
所以基本上，操他的经纪人，在《办公室》第一季把我塞进一个寒酸车里。

415
00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:36.850
I mean, it's a negotiating technique, you know?
我的意思是，这是一种谈判技巧，你知道的？

416
00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:41.390
And they'll be like, well, we can't get you any more money, but we can get you a double
他们会说，好吧，我们没法给你更多片酬，但我们可以给你换成双人

417
00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:42.270
banger instead.
间化妆车。

418
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:44.510
I did not know that.
我以前真不知道。

419
00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:45.390
Yeah.
是啊。

420
00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.310
Oh my gosh, that's ridiculous.
哦天哪，这太荒谬了。

421
00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:48.030
I know.
我知道。

422
00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:49.170
Well, let me tell you a story.
好吧，我给你们讲个故事。

423
00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.650
So I was used to our trailers on The Office.
我以前习惯了我们在《办公室》里的化妆车。

424
00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:56.730
And listen, we didn't have the biggest budget in the early years on The Office.
听着，在《办公室》的前几年，我们的预算不是最充足的。

425
00:20:56.930 --> 00:21:00.870
So even though I was in a double banger trailer, it was old.
所以尽管我住的是双人化妆车，但它很旧。

426
00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:05.070
Like I said, like there was a television, but it wasn't hooked up to anything.
就像我说的，里面有台电视，但没连任何信号。

427
00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:08.270
And like the microwave was iffy, like you said.
就像你说的，微波炉也有点问题。

428
00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:09.250
Oh no, it was dangerous.
噢不，那很危险。

429
00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:13.670
But while I was doing The Office, I got the job on Blades of Glory.
但在拍《办公室》期间，我得到了《冰刀双人组》的工作。

430
00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:16.330
Which is such a big budget movie.
那是一部预算很大的电影。

431
00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:17.670
Huge budget movie.
预算超大的电影。

432
00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:24.570
And they walked me to my trailer, and I didn't know what had happened to me.
他们把我带到我的化妆车前，我都不知道自己遭遇了什么。

433
00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:25.730
Did you just start laughing?
你当时直接笑出来了吗？

434
00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.210
Like, what the hell is this?
就觉得，这到底是个什么鬼？

435
00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:33.530
It was like I had gone from like a middle seat on Southwest to a private jet.
这就好比我从西南航空的中间座位直接跳到了私人飞机上。

436
00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:36.050
Like that was the difference.
这就是差距。

437
00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:39.350
I was like, holy crap.
我当时想，天哪。

438
00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:42.950
I had a full kitchen with an oven.
我有一个带烤箱的完整厨房。

439
00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:47.370
I remember calling my family and being like, should I bake something?
我记得给家人打电话，跟他们说，我是不是该烤点东西？

440
00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:48.730
Like, what do I need this for?
我就想，我要这玩意儿干嘛？

441
00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:53.370
It had a huge flat screen TV hooked up to satellite television.
里面有一台连接了卫星电视的巨型平板电视。

442
00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:55.070
It had a fireplace.
它有一个壁炉。

443
00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:56.910
It had a full bedroom.
它有一间完整的卧室。

444
00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:58.450
It was huge.
太大了。

445
00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:01.010
I like didn't know what to do with myself.
我简直不知道该拿它怎么办才好。

446
00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:03.690
Lady, that would have blown my mind.
莱迪，那绝对会让我大开眼界。

447
00:22:03.810 --> 00:22:08.030
I mean, the nicest trailer I've ever had was this past year when we did AT&T.
我的意思是，我用过的最好的化妆车就是去年我们拍AT&T广告的时候。

448
00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:10.710
I was like, this trailer is bananas.
我当时想，这化妆车太离谱了。

449
00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:20.170
But I sort of love that our show was just not like the big Hollywood hullabaloo, you know?
但我有点喜欢我们的节目不像好莱坞那种大肆喧嚣的制作，你知道吗？

450
00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:20.630
Yeah.
是啊。

451
00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.630
Because we were all really close because of it.
因为经历过这些，我们所有人都变得非常亲密。

452
00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:23.730
We weren't spread apart.
我们没有分散开。

453
00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:28.170
We spent all day on set together in one giant room, basically.
基本上，我们一整天都在片场的一个超大房间里一起度过。

454
00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:32.450
And then our trailers were all right in this little nook in the parking lot.
然后我们的化妆车都停在停车场的一个小角落里。

455
00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:33.950
And you had neighbors.
而且你还有邻居。

456
00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:36.070
You had people right next to you.
你旁边就住着人。

457
00:22:36.230 --> 00:22:38.750
It was like a little community out there.
那感觉就像外面一个小小的社区。

458
00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:45.110
And I have to say, because my trailer was so nice on Blades of Glory, I spent a lot of time in it.
我得说，因为我在《荣誉之刃》里的化妆车太棒了，我在里面花了很多时间。

459
00:22:45.310 --> 00:22:49.610
Like, I watched that TV when I wasn't needed on set.
比如，片场不需要我的时候，我就看那台电视。

460
00:22:49.770 --> 00:22:51.570
I was like, this place is amazing.
当时我就想，这地方太棒了。

461
00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.230
This is, like, better than my house.
这简直比我的房子还要好。

462
00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:55.230
I loved it.
我很喜欢它。

463
00:22:55.730 --> 00:22:57.430
Like, I loved it so much.
真的，我太喜欢它了。

464
00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:04.550
And I think, though, because our trailers were not fancy schmancy, we didn't, like, just hang out in them.
不过我想，正因为我们的化妆车没那么豪华，我们才不会只呆在里面闲逛。

465
00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:11.370
We would come out in the parking lot, and we would play basketball together, or we would chit-chat and make jokes.
我们会去到停车场，一起打篮球，或者闲聊、开玩笑。

466
00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:13.050
Sit on the steps and, like, play music.
坐在台阶上，比如说，放放音乐。

467
00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:16.970
We were more social because we didn't have, like, such great digs.
我们变得更善于社交了，因为我们的住处没那么好。

468
00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:27.150
I do have a really funny story about, you know, when we were doing The Office, my niece and nephews, they all, at different times, graduated high school.
我确实有一个非常有趣的故事，你知道的，当我们拍《办公室》时，我的侄子和外甥们都在不同时期高中毕业了。

469
00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:29.190
Because we did the show for nine years, you know?
因为我们这部剧拍了九年，你知道的？

470
00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:36.370
And so one of the things I would do is I would fly them out, and they would come to set, and they would get a tour of the set, and they'd have lunch with me on set.
所以我会做的一件事就是机票买好让他们飞过来，他们会来片场参观，还会跟我一起在片场吃午饭。

471
00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:42.670
So my one nephew, he's so sweet, my nephew James, when he came out to visit, I was showing him my trailer.
所以我有一个外甥，他特别贴心，我的外甥詹姆斯，当他来探班时，我带他参观了我的化妆车。

472
00:23:42.870 --> 00:23:43.750
And here's the thing.
关键是这样的。

473
00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:45.770
We've said our trailers were older, right?
我们说过我们的化妆车比较旧，对吧？

474
00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:46.110
Yeah.
对。

475
00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:46.510
They were older.
它们比较旧。

476
00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:52.730
There was a decorating theme, there was a motif, and it was southweSt.
里面有一种装饰主题，有一种母题，那就是西南风情。

477
00:23:53.130 --> 00:24:04.410
So depending on what trailer you had, there would be kind of like a fakie painting in a wooden frame that was, like, almost like Jim's clown painting in his parents' house.
所以根据你住的化妆车不同，里面会有一种木框的假画，就像吉姆父母家里那幅小丑画一样。

478
00:24:04.410 --> 00:24:06.010
It was bolted to the wall.
它是用螺栓固定在墙上的。

479
00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:08.310
So, like, there's no moving this picture.
所以，这画根本挪不动。

480
00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:12.890
Whatever trailer you got, there would be a picture, and it would be there no matter what.
不管你分到哪辆化妆车，里面都会有一幅画，而且雷打不动就在那儿。

481
00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:15.910
It was like a wolf, like, howling at the sunset.
就像是一头狼在向着夕阳长嚎。

482
00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:20.130
Seriously, or like cowboys driving home a cattle range of cows.
说真的，或者像牛仔们赶着一群牛在牧场上回家的画。

483
00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:20.510
Yeah.
对。

484
00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:32.590
Or mine was a big sort of clay terracotta pot with, like, etchings on it, like you might see in a cave, you know, of, like, bison or something.
或者我那辆里面是一个巨大的陶土罐，上面有那种你可能在山洞里见过的刻画，比如野牛之类的。

485
00:24:32.690 --> 00:24:33.470
Yes, I remember.
是的，我记得。

486
00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:38.630
And my nephew saw it and was like, oh, that's a cool painting.
我外甥看到了就说，哦，这画挺酷的。

487
00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:39.530
That's pretty cool.
这挺酷的嘛。

488
00:24:39.530 --> 00:24:41.610
You brought that and put that out there.
这是你自带并摆在那儿的吧。

489
00:24:41.610 --> 00:24:43.950
You're like, I did not bring, did not bring.
你就说，我可没带，真没带。

490
00:24:44.090 --> 00:24:46.510
I was like, oh, honey, it's just here.
我就说，哦，亲爱的，这本来就在这儿。

491
00:24:46.650 --> 00:24:47.710
But we did decorate.
不过我们确实装饰过。

492
00:24:48.370 --> 00:24:49.590
We did decorate.
我们确实装饰过。

493
00:24:49.830 --> 00:24:50.230
We did.
我们弄过。

494
00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:50.970
The girls decorated.
女生们进行了装饰。

495
00:24:51.170 --> 00:24:52.530
The boys didn't really decorate.
男生们其实没怎么装饰。

496
00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:53.830
The boys did nothing.
男生们什么都没做。

497
00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:55.890
But, yeah, we decorated a ton.
但是，对，我们装饰得很厉害。

498
00:24:56.010 --> 00:25:00.590
I mean, I had a lamp from home because I love low light.
我是说，我从家里带了一盏灯，因为我喜欢昏暗的灯光。

499
00:25:00.730 --> 00:25:02.950
I'm not a huge fan of, like, overhead fluorescent lights.
我不太喜欢那种头顶上的荧光灯。

500
00:25:03.210 --> 00:25:06.510
And I would have a plant, and I would have a little desk area.
而且我还会放一盆植物，我还会有一个小书桌区域。

501
00:25:06.690 --> 00:25:10.390
Lady, I remember you had made, like, your own little home office nook.
女士，我记得你弄过类似你自己的小家庭办公角落。

502
00:25:10.390 --> 00:25:15.730
Yeah, I also would bring in a pillow and, like, a nice cozy throw blanket.
对，我还会带一个枕头和一条舒适的毯子。

503
00:25:15.910 --> 00:25:17.450
I wanted homey touches.
我想要点家的温馨感。

504
00:25:17.450 --> 00:25:18.970
I wanted it to feel cozy.
我希望它感觉很温馨。

505
00:25:19.210 --> 00:25:24.330
But in answer to your question, Emily, at the end of every season, you had to pack everything up.
但回答你的问题，艾米莉，每一季结束时，你都得把所有东西都打包好。

506
00:25:24.630 --> 00:25:28.210
Like, these trailers were rented from somewhere.
比如，这些拖车都是从某个地方租来的。

507
00:25:28.510 --> 00:25:31.390
And at the end of every season, they get returned.
而且每季结束时，它们都要被归还。

508
00:25:31.390 --> 00:25:33.190
And then we would get a new set.
然后我们会换一辆新的。

509
00:25:33.930 --> 00:25:35.070
But, so, yeah.
所以，是的。

510
00:25:36.090 --> 00:25:40.070
Yeah, it was like, it felt like a college dorm that we had to, like, load in and load out.
对，这就好像，感觉就像大学宿舍，我们不得不搬进搬出。

511
00:25:40.270 --> 00:25:42.270
And that's when the guys would just kind of look at us.
然后男士们就会那样看着我们。

512
00:25:42.350 --> 00:25:44.950
Because on the last day, they would just get in their cars and leave.
因为在最后一天，他们直接上车就走了。

513
00:25:45.330 --> 00:25:47.550
Yeah, and we would have, like, boxes of things.
对，而我们却有一箱箱的东西。

514
00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:49.430
We'd have boxes that we were packing up.
我们有要打包的箱子。

515
00:25:49.550 --> 00:25:50.790
And we would label things.
我们还会给东西贴上标签。

516
00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:55.130
So it would be, like, trailer bedding, trailer desk stuff.
所以上面会写着，比如，拖车床上用品、拖车办公用品。

517
00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:56.030
Yeah.
对。

518
00:25:56.470 --> 00:26:00.190
And Angela, you mentioned that our trailers were located in our parking lot.
安吉拉，你提到过我们的拖车停在停车场里。

519
00:26:00.350 --> 00:26:03.370
And they were kind of, like, in a big configuration.
它们大致呈一个大阵列摆放着。

520
00:26:03.650 --> 00:26:07.830
And it was a pretty easy walk to get to the stage.
而且走到片场非常近。

521
00:26:08.530 --> 00:26:16.070
But sometimes when you're on a show or a movie or on a location, your trailers are actually really far away from the set.
但有时你在拍电视剧、电影或者外景时，你的拖车其实离片场非常远。

522
00:26:16.070 --> 00:26:20.770
And you have to ride in, like, a van or a golf cart or something to get to the set.
你得坐面包车、高尔夫球车之类的交通工具去片场。

523
00:26:20.770 --> 00:26:24.930
But for us, it was like you could walk to the stages.
但对我们来说，就像你可以步行去片场一样。

524
00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:26.190
You could.
确实可以。

525
00:26:26.350 --> 00:26:27.490
But I do want to share something.
不过我确实想分享个事。

526
00:26:27.650 --> 00:26:28.250
And I love this.
而且我太喜欢这个了。

527
00:26:28.370 --> 00:26:29.970
Lady, I reached out to Steve Burgess.
女士，我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

528
00:26:30.110 --> 00:26:31.950
And he sent me some great details I'm going to share in a minute.
他给我发了一些很棒的细节，我一会儿就分享。

529
00:26:32.010 --> 00:26:36.290
But he also sent me a ton of pictures of our trailers just all in a row.
但他还发给我一大堆我们拖车排成一排的照片。

530
00:26:36.850 --> 00:26:38.510
And here's the thing I have to share.
接下来我要分享的是这个。

531
00:26:39.770 --> 00:26:44.150
So, you know, when you're cast on a show, on the call sheet, you're numbered.
你知道的，当你参演一部剧时，通告单上是有编号的。

532
00:26:44.390 --> 00:26:46.070
And so Steve was number one.
所以史蒂夫是一号。

533
00:26:46.210 --> 00:26:46.430
Yes.
没错。

534
00:26:46.450 --> 00:26:49.410
So his trailer was closest to the stage door.
所以他的拖车离片场大门最近。

535
00:26:49.410 --> 00:26:51.710
And Steve had a full-size trailer.
而且史蒂夫有一辆标准尺寸的拖车。

536
00:26:51.830 --> 00:26:55.910
He was the only one of us who had a full trailer all to himself.
他是我们当中唯一一个独占整辆大拖车的人。

537
00:26:56.270 --> 00:26:56.630
Yeah.
对。

538
00:26:56.830 --> 00:26:58.850
But he was the closest to the door.
但他离门最近。

539
00:26:58.910 --> 00:26:59.810
Very close to the door.
离门非常近。

540
00:27:00.210 --> 00:27:02.490
So now I was number eight.
所以我是八号。

541
00:27:02.650 --> 00:27:05.110
So I had a little further walk.
所以我要多走一小段路。

542
00:27:05.250 --> 00:27:06.150
You were down a row.
你在后面一排。

543
00:27:06.430 --> 00:27:06.510
Than you did.
比你远一点。

544
00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:08.130
I was down the row.
我在后面那一排。

545
00:27:08.350 --> 00:27:11.070
And the supporting cast would kind of, like, joke about that.
配角们有时会拿这个开玩笑。

546
00:27:11.210 --> 00:27:12.630
Like, where we were at in the row.
比如我们在队伍里的位置。

547
00:27:12.810 --> 00:27:16.590
Well, that was a crazy thing about our show, which was that our trailers were outside.
好吧，我们这部剧最疯狂的一点就是，我们的拖车是在室外的。

548
00:27:16.590 --> 00:27:20.270
Like, a lot of times, if you're in the fancy studios, you actually don't have trailers.
比如很多时候，如果你在豪华的制片厂里，你其实是没有拖车的。

549
00:27:20.390 --> 00:27:21.350
You have dressing rooMs.
你有专属的化妆间。

550
00:27:21.610 --> 00:27:23.750
And they're, like, attached to your stage.
而且它们就像是连在你拍戏的摄影棚上的。

551
00:27:23.790 --> 00:27:26.210
And so you're, like, indoors the whole time.
所以你差不多整天都在室内。

552
00:27:26.670 --> 00:27:31.990
But our hair and makeup, where we got ready for hair and makeup, was a giant trailer out in the parking lot.
但是我们的发型和化妆间——我们做发型和化妆的地方，是停车场里的一个巨型拖车。

553
00:27:32.090 --> 00:27:37.050
So on those rainy days, I remember how frustrated hair and makeup would be, particularly hair.
所以在那些下雨天，我记得发型和化妆部门会有多沮丧，尤其是发型部门。

554
00:27:37.230 --> 00:27:39.290
Because they'd be like, well, I'm going to get you all ready.
因为他们会觉得，好吧，我要把你们的造型都做好。

555
00:27:39.290 --> 00:27:42.350
And now you're just going to walk in the rain to your trailer and get dressed.
然后你就要顶着雨走到你的拖车里去换衣服。

556
00:27:42.490 --> 00:27:45.670
And then you're going to walk in the rain again to get to the stages.
接着你还要再顶着雨走到片场去。

557
00:27:45.670 --> 00:27:48.270
By the time you get there, I'm just going to have to start all over again.
等你们到了那里，我就只能一切从头再来。

558
00:27:48.830 --> 00:27:49.190
Yes.
没错。

559
00:27:49.410 --> 00:27:52.610
Well, now I want to share with you this email I got from Steve Burgess.
好了，现在我想和你们分享这封我从史蒂夫·伯吉斯那里收到的电子邮件。

560
00:27:52.870 --> 00:27:55.110
You know, we trade emails, Jenna and I, and Steve.
你知道的，我们会互相发邮件，珍娜和我，还有史蒂夫。

561
00:27:55.270 --> 00:27:57.950
And he sends us pictures from his life in Tennessee.
他会给我们发他在田纳西州生活时的照片。

562
00:27:58.050 --> 00:27:59.550
And we sent him pictures back.
我们也会回发照片给他。

563
00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:01.090
He's just the most wonderful person.
他真的是个最棒的人。

564
00:28:01.710 --> 00:28:05.450
And so I was emailing him about Isabel turning 18, you know.
所以我就发邮件问他伊莎贝尔快要满18岁的事，你知道的。

565
00:28:06.030 --> 00:28:07.990
And so we had started this back and forth.
于是我们就这样一来一回地聊了起来。

566
00:28:08.010 --> 00:28:14.230
And I said, hey, while we're chatting, do you have any memories of our base camp and our trailers?
然后我说，嘿，趁我们正聊着，你对我们的大本营和拖车有什么记忆吗？

567
00:28:14.470 --> 00:28:17.470
Because we got this really fun fan question, and we're going to talk about it.
因为我们收到了一个非常有趣的粉丝提问，我们打算聊聊这个。

568
00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:23.430
And I also asked him, how many trailers at any given time did we have in that parking lot?
我还问了他，在任何特定时间，我们在那个停车场里到底有多少辆拖车？

569
00:28:23.630 --> 00:28:25.570
And so here's some of the stuff he wrote back.
所以这里有些是他回信写的内容。

570
00:28:25.590 --> 00:28:25.990
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

571
00:28:26.110 --> 00:28:26.430
I am.
准备好了。

572
00:28:26.730 --> 00:28:30.490
First of all, he said about our trailers, they weren't a four-star hotel.
首先，关于我们的拖车，他说它们可不是什么四星级酒店。

573
00:28:31.070 --> 00:28:33.670
But they were okay to survive in while not on set.
但不在片场时，在里面凑合度日还是可以的。

574
00:28:33.670 --> 00:28:38.390
By the time I joined the office, it was season six, and everyone was pretty settled in their trailers.
等我加入《办公室》剧组时已经是第六季了，大家都已经在各自的拖车里安顿得差不多了。

575
00:28:39.570 --> 00:28:42.710
And then I asked him about what happened when we would go on location.
然后我问了他当我们外出外景时会发生什么。

576
00:28:43.290 --> 00:28:45.490
He said, for the most part, it was manageable.
他说，基本上，这都还在掌控之中。

577
00:28:45.790 --> 00:28:48.550
But other times, our base camp looked like a small city.
但有时，我们的大本营看起来就像一座小城市。

578
00:28:48.790 --> 00:28:53.890
We tried to keep things small when we were just going out for a day or two with only a few cast members.
当我们要外出拍摄一两天、只有少数几位演员时，我们会尽量保持规模精简。

579
00:28:54.150 --> 00:28:59.990
But when the whole cast was on location, we had to bring everyone's trailer, plus trailers for guest stars.
但当全体演员都在外景地时，我们必须把每个人的拖车都带上，还要加上客串演员的拖车。

580
00:28:59.990 --> 00:29:04.650
We also had to have a cast trailer for the director, usually one for the writer as well.
我们还得为导演准备一辆演员拖车，通常还要为编剧准备一辆。

581
00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:11.490
And then in addition to the cast trailers, we had to have costume props, grip, electric, hair, makeup, ADs, catering, and transportation.
除了演员拖车之外，我们还得有服装、道具、灯光、电力、发型、化妆、副导演、餐饮和交通车。

582
00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:14.090
So here is an example.
所以这里有一个例子。

583
00:29:14.290 --> 00:29:19.530
On the christening episode, we shot at a church in Pasadena with the whole entire caSt.
在洗礼那一集，我们在帕萨迪纳的一座教堂拍摄，全体演员都在。

584
00:29:19.530 --> 00:29:21.850
This is what was set up at our base camp.
这就是我们大本营当时的配置。

585
00:29:22.430 --> 00:29:33.450
Four single trailers, three double-banger trailers, four triple-banger trailers, one honey wagon, a camera truck, a grip truck, a lightning truck, a set dressing truck,
四辆单间拖车，三辆双拼拖车，四辆三拼拖车，一辆多功能车，一辆摄像卡车，一辆道具卡车，一辆灯光卡车，一辆布景卡车，

586
00:29:33.570 --> 00:29:42.410
a wardrobe trailer, a hair and makeup trailer, a catering truck, six vans, seven steak bed trucks, two people boovers, which are 30-person buses,
一辆服装拖车，一辆发型和化妆拖车，一辆餐饮卡车，六辆面包车，七辆平板卡车，两辆人员摆渡车，也就是30人的大巴，

587
00:29:42.410 --> 00:29:51.750
one drivable generator, one tractor with a generator, because the tractor pulled the wardrobe trailer, which was a 40-foot semi when they were connected, one church bus,
一台可移动发电机，一台带发电机的拖拉机，因为当它们连接在一起时，拖拉机拉着的是一辆40英尺长的半挂服装拖车，一辆教堂大巴，

588
00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:52.770
and Jim's car.
还有吉姆的车。

589
00:29:53.470 --> 00:29:54.070
Wow.
哇。

590
00:29:54.850 --> 00:29:56.550
That was for the christening episode.
那可是为了洗礼那一集。

591
00:29:56.710 --> 00:29:57.610
Isn't that unreal?
这简直太不真实了吧？

592
00:29:58.130 --> 00:29:58.470
Yeah.
是啊。

593
00:29:58.470 --> 00:29:59.190
It's amazing.
太惊人了。

594
00:29:59.470 --> 00:30:00.290
That's amazing.
这太惊人了。

595
00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:09.130
That's something I didn't know if people knew, which is that, like, the point of the trailers is that if we ever went on location, they would just hitch them up and move them.
有件事我不知道大家是否清楚，那就是，拖车的意义在于，如果我们去外景地，他们就可以直接把它们挂上钩然后运走。

596
00:30:09.230 --> 00:30:16.330
So, like, my dressing room with all its decor and everything that I liked to keep in it would be over at that church that morning.
所以，比如我的化妆间，带着它所有的装饰以及我喜欢放在里面的所有东西，那天早上就会出现在那座教堂旁边。

597
00:30:16.570 --> 00:30:17.630
Yeah, exactly.
对，完全正确。

598
00:30:17.950 --> 00:30:23.390
And he sent pictures from when we did the finale, and our base camp does look like a small city.
他还发了我们拍大结局时的照片，我们的大本营看起来真的像一座小城市。

599
00:30:23.590 --> 00:30:25.870
And it rained, and he sent me a picture.
而且当时下雨了，他还发给我一张照片。

600
00:30:26.090 --> 00:30:29.950
It was like a mud hole that we had to, like, wade through to get to the food.
那就像是个泥坑，我们得像那样蹚过去才能拿到食物。

601
00:30:30.290 --> 00:30:30.510
Yeah.
是啊。

602
00:30:30.670 --> 00:30:31.150
Yeah.
是啊。

603
00:30:31.370 --> 00:30:32.130
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

604
00:30:32.470 --> 00:30:40.470
You know, another question that I think people wonder about a lot, at least people have asked me, is how much time we spent in our trailers and how private they are.
你知道的，我觉得大家经常好奇的另一个问题，至少也有人问过我，就是我们在化妆车里呆了多长时间，它们有多注重隐私。

605
00:30:40.750 --> 00:30:42.470
Oh, well, they're not private.
哦，其实一点都不注重隐私。

606
00:30:42.790 --> 00:30:45.770
If you share a wall, it's not private, just so you know.
如果你跟别人共用一堵墙，那就完全没有隐私，提醒你一下。

607
00:30:45.950 --> 00:30:52.030
But even if you do have, like, a trailer to yourself, it's still not totally a private space.
但就算你真的有属于自己的化妆车，它也算不上完全是个人的私人空间。

608
00:30:52.030 --> 00:30:56.250
There is always someone knocking on your door, entering your trailer.
总是有人敲你的门，走进你的化妆车。

609
00:30:56.590 --> 00:31:00.070
They are constantly delivering new clothes.
他们一直在送来新衣服。

610
00:31:00.290 --> 00:31:01.230
Or script pages.
或者是剧本页。

611
00:31:01.250 --> 00:31:02.370
Or memos.
或者是备忘录。

612
00:31:03.210 --> 00:31:05.550
If you do share a wall, the walls are thin.
如果你真的共用一堵墙，那墙是很薄的。

613
00:31:06.390 --> 00:31:06.570
Yeah.
对。

614
00:31:06.710 --> 00:31:09.970
In the first season of The Office, I shared a wall with BJ.
在《办公室》的第一季，我和BJ共用一堵墙。

615
00:31:10.370 --> 00:31:13.330
I had a double banger, and he was my trailer mate.
我住的是双拼化妆车，他成了我的隔壁邻居。

616
00:31:13.770 --> 00:31:17.850
John and Rain were paired together, and then BJ and I were paired together.
约翰和雷恩被分到了一起，然后我和BJ被分到了一起。

617
00:31:18.030 --> 00:31:19.950
And BJ would listen to music.
而且BJ总是听音乐。

618
00:31:19.950 --> 00:31:28.470
And when we moved, I said I didn't want to share a wall with BJ anymore.
等我们搬了地方，我说我再也不想跟BJ共用一堵墙了。

619
00:31:29.550 --> 00:31:31.470
I kicked him out.
我把他给踢出去了。

620
00:31:31.650 --> 00:31:34.490
I was like, I don't want to listen to your music.
我说，我可不想听你的音乐。

621
00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:35.910
It's so loud.
声音太大了。

622
00:31:35.910 --> 00:31:36.890
It's so loud.
声音太大了。

623
00:31:37.030 --> 00:31:41.550
Here's the other thing I remember about BJ being your neighbor was that I would come
关于BJ做你邻居，我还记得另一件事，那就是我有时会

624
00:31:41.550 --> 00:31:48.270
in and hang out with you, and we could hear him lift the toilet seat to go pee because
走进来跟你一起玩，我们能听到他掀起马桶盖去小便，因为

625
00:31:48.270 --> 00:31:51.670
he would fling it open, and it would whack the wall.
他会猛地把它推开，然后撞到墙上。

626
00:31:51.810 --> 00:31:54.770
And the first time I was in there when it happened, it startled me.
第一次发生这事的时候我在里面，吓了我一跳。

627
00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:56.430
And I was like, what was that noise?
我说，那是什么声音？

628
00:31:56.430 --> 00:31:59.230
And you said, I think it's when he goes pee.
你说，我猜是他去小便的时候。

629
00:31:59.590 --> 00:32:02.230
He flings the lid open.
他把马桶盖猛地甩开了。

630
00:32:02.470 --> 00:32:02.870
Yes.
对。

631
00:32:03.010 --> 00:32:04.790
He was loud.
他动静很大。

632
00:32:05.830 --> 00:32:06.790
And so—
所以——

633
00:32:06.790 --> 00:32:07.710
We love you, BJ.
我们爱你，BJ。

634
00:32:07.890 --> 00:32:08.550
We love you.
我们爱你。

635
00:32:08.690 --> 00:32:08.950
We love you, BJ.
我们爱你，BJ。

636
00:32:09.290 --> 00:32:11.090
You were really loud over there.
你在那边动静真的很大。

637
00:32:11.450 --> 00:32:16.330
But, you know, you spent as much time in your trailer as you needed to change your clothes,
不过呢，你在化妆车里呆的时间，也就是换衣服需要的时间，

638
00:32:16.330 --> 00:32:20.830
or if you weren't in a scene, that's where you might go hang out.
或者如果没你的戏份，你可能会去那里呆着消磨时间。

639
00:32:21.290 --> 00:32:21.690
Yeah.
对。

640
00:32:21.990 --> 00:32:24.430
And Emily asked us, were we able to pick our neighbors?
艾米莉问我们，我们能不能自己挑邻居？

641
00:32:24.570 --> 00:32:25.730
And the answer to that is no.
答案是不能。

642
00:32:25.730 --> 00:32:30.650
Well, I didn't get to pick who I wanted as my neighbor, but I was able to pick who I didn't
好吧，我没能挑自己想选的邻居，但我大概能挑我

643
00:32:30.650 --> 00:32:31.550
want, I guess.
不想选的人。

644
00:32:31.730 --> 00:32:32.090
I did.
我确实挑了。

645
00:32:32.110 --> 00:32:32.990
I guess that's true.
我想也是这样。

646
00:32:33.110 --> 00:32:34.870
Say, please, no more.
求求了，别再来了。

647
00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:38.750
Well, as you all know, Kate Flannery was my first neighbor.
好吧，如大家所知，凯特·弗兰内里是我的第一个邻居。

648
00:32:39.070 --> 00:32:44.570
And then my second neighbor was Phyllis, and she was amazing because she's so quiet.
然后我的第二个邻居是菲利丝，她太棒了，因为她特别安静。

649
00:32:44.990 --> 00:32:49.890
So if you have to pick someone on the office cast to be your neighbor, I highly recommend
所以如果你必须在《办公室》演员里挑一个人当邻居，我强烈推荐

650
00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:50.310
Phyllis.
菲利丝。

651
00:32:50.610 --> 00:32:55.250
Also, the trailer next to me, so like my windows faced their windows.
还有，我隔壁的拖车，我的窗户正对着他们的窗户。

652
00:32:55.730 --> 00:32:56.750
Was Ed HelMs.
是艾德·赫尔姆斯（Ed Helms）。

653
00:32:56.890 --> 00:32:57.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

654
00:32:57.250 --> 00:33:01.370
And he would play the banjo, and I would open my window so I could hear him playing the
他会弹班卓琴，我会打开窗户听他弹

655
00:33:01.370 --> 00:33:02.890
banjo, and I loved it.
班卓琴，我太喜欢了。

656
00:33:03.050 --> 00:33:07.170
So, lady, Ed's trailer was in between mine and yours.
所以，女士，艾德的拖车就在我和你之间。

657
00:33:07.630 --> 00:33:08.070
Yes.
是的。

658
00:33:08.430 --> 00:33:10.610
Because he was also my kind of neighbor.
因为他也是我的邻居那种。

659
00:33:11.270 --> 00:33:13.630
You know, I didn't share a wall with him, but yes.
你知道的，我没跟他共用一堵墙，但确实是。

660
00:33:13.630 --> 00:33:17.290
And I could hear his banjo as well, and I loved it.
我也能听到他的班卓琴声，我好喜欢。

661
00:33:17.450 --> 00:33:18.230
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

662
00:33:18.290 --> 00:33:23.370
I loved it so much that sometimes if I had a little bit more downtime and like maybe I
我太喜欢了，有时候如果我有更多空闲时间，比如可能

663
00:33:23.370 --> 00:33:29.610
would take a little cat nap, I would sort of wake to Ed's banjo playing, and I made it
小睡一会儿，我就会伴着艾德的班卓琴声醒来，我把它

664
00:33:29.610 --> 00:33:31.430
my alarm on my cell phone.
设成了手机闹钟。

665
00:33:31.590 --> 00:33:33.410
It's like very nostalgic for me.
这对我来说非常有情怀。

666
00:33:33.510 --> 00:33:35.550
Like if you're going to wake me up, play the banjo.
就像如果你非要叫醒我，那就弹班卓琴吧。

667
00:33:35.710 --> 00:33:35.830
Yeah.
是啊。

668
00:33:35.830 --> 00:33:37.490
And then I don't wake up so grumpy.
然后我就不会那么起床气了。

669
00:33:38.030 --> 00:33:39.190
John's trailer was loud.
约翰的拖车可真吵。

670
00:33:39.190 --> 00:33:40.210
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

671
00:33:40.410 --> 00:33:41.790
John's trailer was so loud.
约翰的拖车太吵了。

672
00:33:42.130 --> 00:33:43.810
I don't know what they did in there.
我不知道他们在里面干嘛。

673
00:33:43.970 --> 00:33:48.270
I think they would just yell at the TV or yell at each other when like the Madden football
我觉得他们就是对着电视大喊大叫，或者当《麦登橄榄球》

674
00:33:48.270 --> 00:33:49.530
was going nutso.
玩得火热时互相大喊大叫。

675
00:33:49.710 --> 00:33:49.950
Yeah.
是啊。

676
00:33:50.350 --> 00:33:51.750
And so it would shake.
而且它还会震动。

677
00:33:52.010 --> 00:33:52.110
Yeah.
是啊。

678
00:33:52.210 --> 00:33:55.730
You would walk by John's trailer, and it would be moving, and it'd be because like
你路过约翰的拖车时，它甚至在动，那是因为

679
00:33:56.390 --> 00:33:58.150
Brian Baumgartner was like, you know.
布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳（Brian Baumgartner）在里面，你知道的。

680
00:33:58.150 --> 00:33:59.030
Jumping up and down in there.
在里面上蹿下跳。

681
00:33:59.070 --> 00:33:59.970
Jumping up and down or something.
上蹿下跳之类的。

682
00:34:00.190 --> 00:34:00.610
Yes, they would.
对，他们会的。

683
00:34:00.730 --> 00:34:01.590
They would jump up and down.
他们会上蹿下跳。

684
00:34:01.690 --> 00:34:04.570
And sometimes we would go in there, and we would just sit and hang out.
有时候我们会进去，坐在那儿闲晃。

685
00:34:04.690 --> 00:34:05.490
And watch them.
看着他们。

686
00:34:05.670 --> 00:34:05.970
Yeah.
是啊。

687
00:34:06.350 --> 00:34:07.750
If we were like really bored.
如果我们实在无聊的话。

688
00:34:07.750 --> 00:34:11.250
If we were really bored, we'd say, let's go see what the boys are doing.
如果我们实在无聊，就会说，去看看这帮小子在干嘛。

689
00:34:11.470 --> 00:34:11.810
Exactly.
没错。

690
00:34:11.810 --> 00:34:14.230
And they were just yelling at each other in the TV.
然后他们就在那儿冲着电视和彼此大喊大叫。

691
00:34:14.510 --> 00:34:17.970
And you could hear them walking through the parking lot like, what the hell?
你能听到他们走过停车场时喊着：搞什么鬼？

692
00:34:18.150 --> 00:34:19.070
Come on, man.
拜托，老兄。

693
00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:19.850
Yes.
是的。

694
00:34:20.150 --> 00:34:27.310
But, lady, we have to share that when we had kids, we graduated to a very special trailer
但是，女士，我们不得不分享一下，当我们有了孩子后，我们升级到了一种非常特殊的拖车

695
00:34:27.310 --> 00:34:27.910
configuration.
配置。

696
00:34:28.190 --> 00:34:31.130
This was a time when you really led the way.
那时候你真的是带头人。

697
00:34:31.530 --> 00:34:36.270
They were so wonderful for you when you brought Isabel back after our hiatus.
在我们假期结束后，你把伊莎贝尔（Isabel）带回来时，它们对你太好了。

698
00:34:36.270 --> 00:34:41.970
So I had Isabel right after Goodbye, Toby, because I was super pregnant.
所以我拍完《再见，托比》（Goodbye, Toby）就生下伊莎贝尔了，因为我当时超级显怀。

699
00:34:42.350 --> 00:34:43.950
They couldn't even hide my belly anymore.
他们甚至再也遮不住我的肚子了。

700
00:34:43.950 --> 00:34:47.650
If you watch that episode when Andy proposes to Angela, you can just see my belly.
如果你看安迪向安吉拉求婚的那集，你一眼就能看到我的肚子。

701
00:34:47.790 --> 00:34:47.930
They gave up.
他们放弃了。

702
00:34:47.990 --> 00:34:49.110
Because they gave up.
因为他们放弃了。

703
00:34:49.350 --> 00:34:52.410
And I had her like, what, lady, like eight days later?
而且我大概是在，什么来着，女士，大概八天后就把她生下来了？

704
00:34:52.610 --> 00:34:52.770
Yeah.
对。

705
00:34:52.890 --> 00:34:53.290
Something crazy.
有点疯狂。

706
00:34:53.870 --> 00:34:59.930
And so when I came back to set for season five, I had this newborn.
所以当我回到第五季的片场时，我已经有了这个新生儿。

707
00:35:00.130 --> 00:35:04.110
And at first, I would just have her in the trailer with me.
起初，我只是让她和我待在化妆车里。

708
00:35:04.250 --> 00:35:09.350
But like you said, so many people knock throughout the day that I would just kind of be putting
但就像你说的，一整天都有好多人敲门，以至于我好不容易才让她

709
00:35:09.350 --> 00:35:10.250
her down for a nap.
睡个午觉。

710
00:35:10.270 --> 00:35:11.610
And I'd have a break at lunch.
而且我午休时有点时间。

711
00:35:11.710 --> 00:35:13.230
And I was going to have that cozy time with her.
我本打算和她度过那段温馨的时光。

712
00:35:13.310 --> 00:35:14.250
And someone would knock on the door.
然后就会有人敲门。

713
00:35:14.430 --> 00:35:14.570
Right.
没错了。

714
00:35:14.650 --> 00:35:15.330
And she'd wake up.
她就会醒来。

715
00:35:15.330 --> 00:35:18.490
So I remember having this conversation with Randy Cordray.
所以我记得我和兰迪·科德雷有过这样一次谈话。

716
00:35:18.670 --> 00:35:19.730
He was so sweet.
他真是太好了。

717
00:35:19.950 --> 00:35:20.830
He was our producer.
他是我们的制片人。

718
00:35:21.090 --> 00:35:24.250
And he was like, Angela, is there anything you need for the baby?
他说，安吉拉，宝宝有什么需要的东西吗？

719
00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:25.150
How's it going?
进展怎么样？

720
00:35:25.330 --> 00:35:26.950
You know, being back at work with her.
你知道的，带着她回到工作岗位上。

721
00:35:27.370 --> 00:35:28.410
What would be helpful?
有什么能帮上忙的？

722
00:35:28.670 --> 00:35:33.070
And I said, well, I said, when people knock on my door, it wakes her up.
我说，嗯，我说，当人们敲我的门时，会把她吵醒。

