1019
00:49:37.620 --> 00:49:41.900
I had to film a comedy television show and I wasn't in a great mood.
我得拍一部喜剧电视剧，而我当时心情并不好。

1020
00:49:41.900 --> 00:49:47.500
My grandmother passed away while we were shooting the show and I got that news while I was at
在我们拍摄这部剧期间，我奶奶去世了，我在工作时得知了这个消息，

1021
00:49:47.500 --> 00:49:50.420
work and that was hard.
那真的很艰难。

1022
00:49:50.640 --> 00:49:56.040
It was hard to just go sit in laughter after that for the rest of that day.
在那之后的那天剩余时间里，要强颜欢笑真的很不容易。

1023
00:49:56.220 --> 00:49:56.560
Yeah.
是的。

1024
00:49:56.680 --> 00:50:02.440
I remember being very thankful in particular for our cast and how much we were there for
我记得特别感谢我们的演员阵容，以及我们彼此之间是多么地支持对方，因为我们所有人都有过那样的时候。

1025
00:50:02.440 --> 00:50:05.440
each other because we all had times, you know, like that.
因为我们都有过那样的时候。

1026
00:50:05.600 --> 00:50:10.320
And I think on some sets you might not have that kind of support in the way that we had.
我想在某些片场，你可能不会拥有我们那种的支持方式。

1027
00:50:10.320 --> 00:50:15.740
But in the early season of the office, early in season two, my mom was very sick and she
但《办公室》早期第二季的时候，我妈妈病得很重，

1028
00:50:15.740 --> 00:50:18.580
was in the hospital and things were touch and go.
她当时在医院，情况十分危急。

1029
00:50:18.780 --> 00:50:21.960
She ended up, you know, pulling through, but it was very scary.
最后她挺过来了，但当时真的很吓人。

1030
00:50:22.480 --> 00:50:26.180
And I just remember you and Kate just rallying around me.
我只记得你和凯特都围在我身边支持我。

1031
00:50:26.200 --> 00:50:32.720
And you do, you have to just kind of dig deep inside yourself and do your job, you know?
确实如此，你必须从内心深处挖掘力量，做好你的工作，对吧？

1032
00:50:32.920 --> 00:50:36.360
And those are the days where it is just kind of a job, you know?
而那些日子里，它真的就只是一份工作，你知道吗？

1033
00:50:36.360 --> 00:50:41.540
Well, but also, Layla, the part of your question where you said, does sometimes, does it actually
不过，莱拉，你问题中提到的那部分，你说有时候，它真的能让你振作起来吗？

1034
00:50:41.540 --> 00:50:42.420
cheer you up?
它真的能让你振作起来吗？

1035
00:50:42.880 --> 00:50:49.780
There had been mornings where nothing in particular bad or anything scary was happening, but maybe
有些早晨，并没有发生什么特别糟糕或吓人的事情，但可能

1036
00:50:49.780 --> 00:50:54.960
you just had a frazzled morning getting out the door and you're just in that kind of mood
你出门时手忙脚乱，正处于那种情绪中，

1037
00:50:54.960 --> 00:50:58.120
where you walk onto set and you're just like, well, okay, now what?
当你走进片场时，你就会想，好吧，现在又怎么了？

1038
00:50:58.120 --> 00:51:05.200
And then we would have a scene and Steve Carell as Michael would do that laugh that he does
然后我们就会拍一场戏，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔饰演的迈克尔会发出那种他在表演时的笑声，

1039
00:51:05.200 --> 00:51:07.380
when he acts, his acting laugh.
他那独特的演技笑声。

1040
00:51:07.560 --> 00:51:09.280
And it's so damn funny.
真的太好笑了。

1041
00:51:09.500 --> 00:51:14.480
I would find myself laughing or trying not to laugh because my character could never really
我会发现自己忍不住笑出来，或者极力克制不笑，因为我的角色永远不能真正地

1042
00:51:14.480 --> 00:51:15.560
bust out laughing.
放声大笑。

1043
00:51:15.800 --> 00:51:20.700
But there were so many times when Steve pretending to laugh cheered me up.
但有很多次，史蒂夫假装大笑都让我振作了起来。

1044
00:51:20.700 --> 00:51:21.980
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1045
00:51:22.300 --> 00:51:27.700
I mean, I think overall, it was such a beneficial place to work.
我的意思是，我觉得总的来说，这是一个非常棒的工作环境。

1046
00:51:27.700 --> 00:51:35.060
To go into a place where your job was being around comedy and making comedy, it did affect
去一个以喜剧和创作喜剧为工作的地方，它确实影响了

1047
00:51:35.060 --> 00:51:35.660
my mood.
我的心情。

1048
00:51:35.840 --> 00:51:42.120
And I remember I would think, gosh, I often leave work in a happier mood than when I got
我记得我会想，天哪，我离开工作时的心情往往比刚到那里时还要好，

1049
00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:45.220
there just by virtue of having laughed all day.
仅仅因为一整天都在大笑。

1050
00:51:45.220 --> 00:51:51.760
And I thought, what's it like to play a character on a drama where you're dealing with like intense
我想，去演一部正剧里的角色会是什么感觉，你得处理那些激烈的情绪

1051
00:51:51.760 --> 00:51:56.200
subject matter all day or you have to cry all day or you have to have like an intense
整天都在处理沉重的主题，或者你得整天哭泣，或者你必须经历那种极其强烈的

1052
00:51:56.200 --> 00:51:56.560
scene?
场景？

1053
00:51:56.720 --> 00:51:59.760
Because that gets into the fiber of you, you know?
因为这会渗入你的骨髓，你知道吗？

1054
00:51:59.860 --> 00:52:05.120
It's like it's pretend, but you are accessing things in order to bring it forward.
这就像是假装的，但为了把情绪调动起来，你确实在调动内心的某些东西。

1055
00:52:05.480 --> 00:52:10.320
Or exposing yourself to things if it's like subject matter that's really troubling, you know?
或者如果是那种真的很让人困扰的主题，你得让自己暴露在那种情绪中，你知道吗？

1056
00:52:10.420 --> 00:52:10.540
Yes.
对。

1057
00:52:10.860 --> 00:52:11.320
Yes.
是的。

1058
00:52:11.540 --> 00:52:11.740
Yeah.
对啊。

1059
00:52:11.740 --> 00:52:18.900
It's funny, when we did our rewatch, you know that episode where Pam and Jim, they go to buy
说来有趣，当我们重看剧集时，你知道那一集吗，就是帕姆和吉姆去买

1060
00:52:18.900 --> 00:52:20.040
stuff to cheer up Kevin.
东西来让凯文开心。

1061
00:52:20.140 --> 00:52:21.140
It's Michael's birthday.
那是迈克尔的生日。

1062
00:52:21.380 --> 00:52:23.080
But everyone's worried about Kevin.
但所有人都很担心凯文。

1063
00:52:23.220 --> 00:52:24.160
Everyone's worried about Kevin.
所有人都很担心凯文。

1064
00:52:24.380 --> 00:52:29.160
And Pam has her little thing where she's like, Luke, I am your father.
帕姆有个小桥段，她模仿着说：卢克，我是你父亲。

1065
00:52:29.460 --> 00:52:30.620
She does the whole thing.
她把整段都演出来了。

1066
00:52:31.120 --> 00:52:39.420
So that day that we filmed in that store, I won't share why, but I was pretty down that
所以在那个商店拍摄的那天，我不会说原因，但我那天心情相当低落。

1067
00:52:39.420 --> 00:52:39.720
day.
我当时情绪不太好。

1068
00:52:39.720 --> 00:52:41.940
I wasn't in a good mood.
我记得我当时还担心你可能会从我的表演中看出这一点。

1069
00:52:41.940 --> 00:52:46.040
And I remembered worrying that you might see it in my performance.
而当我们重看那集时，我想，不对，我觉得如果我不知情的话，我是绝对看不出来的。

1070
00:52:46.280 --> 00:52:49.820
And when we did the rewatch, I thought, no, I think if I didn't know, I would know.
但不管出于什么原因，那天要进入状态真的很艰难。

1071
00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:54.640
But for whatever reason, that was a tough one that day to go in.
而且因为我必须表现得搞笑，比如我得很有活力、情绪高涨、带着调侃又搞笑，但我

1072
00:52:54.740 --> 00:53:01.200
And because I had to be funny, like I had to be peppy and up and flirty and funny, and I
当时完全没有那种感觉。

1073
00:53:01.200 --> 00:53:02.380
was not feeling it.
不过我觉得我掩饰过去了。

1074
00:53:02.380 --> 00:53:04.220
But I think I covered.
我觉得你掩饰得很好。

1075
00:53:04.900 --> 00:53:05.980
I think you did.
我觉得你表现得棒极了。

1076
00:53:06.220 --> 00:53:07.360
I think you did fantastic.
是啊。

1077
00:53:07.880 --> 00:53:08.060
Yeah.
对啊。

1078
00:53:08.200 --> 00:53:13.420
I think the hardest thing for me, Layla, was the reverse, which is playing a grump around
我觉得对我来说最难的事，蕾拉，正好相反，那就是在一群非常搞笑的人中间扮演一个脾气暴躁的人。

1079
00:53:13.420 --> 00:53:15.160
a lot of really funny people.
因为我想笑，我也在笑，而且我无时无刻不在

1080
00:53:16.640 --> 00:53:21.680
Because I wanted to laugh, and I was laughing, and I was trying to suppress laughter all the
努力强忍着笑意。

1081
00:53:21.680 --> 00:53:22.100
time.
而且，你知道，我得说，珍娜，有些工作就是这样，有时你带着一堆心事来上班，

1082
00:53:22.500 --> 00:53:28.060
And, you know, I will say, Jenna, talk about a job where sometimes you come to work and
但结束一天的工作离开时，你的心情会变得更好。

1083
00:53:28.060 --> 00:53:32.560
you've just got a lot going on, but then you leave at the end of your workday happier.
对我来说，和你以及我们的播客就是这样。

1084
00:53:32.580 --> 00:53:35.480
And that is true for me with you and our podcaSt.
哦，没错。

1085
00:53:35.480 --> 00:53:36.740
Oh, yeah.
很多次当我们录音结束时，尤其是我们在录音室的时候，刚一录完，

1086
00:53:37.260 --> 00:53:43.180
So many times when we're done recording, especially when we're in studio, the minute we're done,
我们就会一起走到车旁，一路走一路聊，聊个没完没了，

1087
00:53:43.360 --> 00:53:48.960
we walk to our cars together, we talk the whole entire way, we have a whole chat session,
就站在其中一辆车旁边聊天，然后我们上车开车回家，

1088
00:53:49.220 --> 00:53:55.000
like standing next to one of our cars, and then we get in our cars and we drive home, and
在开回家的路上，我们要么给对方留个言，要么给对方打电话。

1089
00:53:55.000 --> 00:53:58.700
we either leave each other a message or call each other on the drive home.
我是说，这感觉就像回到了片场一样。

1090
00:53:58.860 --> 00:54:01.040
I mean, it's just like being back on the set.
我懂。

1091
00:54:01.280 --> 00:54:02.020
I know.
我知道。

1092
00:54:02.220 --> 00:54:02.780
I know.
所以我太喜欢了。

1093
00:54:03.080 --> 00:54:04.260
So I love it.
我太喜欢和你一起做这个播客了，老朋友。

1094
00:54:04.260 --> 00:54:06.200
I love doing this podcast with you, lady.
谢谢。

1095
00:54:06.900 --> 00:54:07.340
Thanks.
我也是。

1096
00:54:07.860 --> 00:54:08.380
Me too.
噢。

1097
00:54:08.940 --> 00:54:09.220
Aw.
好了，各位，非常感谢你们。

1098
00:54:09.520 --> 00:54:11.560
Well, you guys, thank you so much.
对我们来说，这是一次充满乐趣的回忆之旅。

1099
00:54:11.700 --> 00:54:13.740
This was a fun trip down memory lane for us.
我们有很多精彩的幕后照片，我会把它们发到动态里，分享我们那段

